# Google Workspace Drive

## When to use

User asked to find, list, read, create, copy, upload, move, share, or audit
Drive files/folders (including Shared Drives). Prefer a connected Google
Workspace MCP.

## MCP tool map

Pass `user_google_email` as the connected MCP documents (example pattern:
`admin@nodadyoushutup.com`). Never invent file or folder ids — resolve via
search/list/get.

| Job | Tools |
| --- | --- |
| Search by name/query | `search_drive_files` (`query`, optional `file_type`,
  `drive_id`, `corpora`, `page_size`, `detailed`) |
| List folder / drive | `list_drive_items` (optional `folder_id`, `drive_id`,
  `query`, `file_type`, `resource_type`, `detailed`) |
| Read file text / metadata content | `get_drive_file_content` (`file_id`) |
| Download / export URL | `get_drive_file_download_url` (`file_id`, optional
  `export_format`) — do not paste binary blobs into chat |
| Permissions inventory | `get_drive_file_permissions` (`file_id`);
  `manage_drive_access` with `action=list` |
| Public / link exposure check | `check_drive_file_public_access`
  (`file_name`, optional `drive_id`) |
| Existing shareable link | `get_drive_shareable_link` (`file_id`) — read of
  current link; enabling anyone-with-link is a mutate |
| Create file | `create_drive_file` (`file_name`, optional `content`,
  `folder_id`, `mime_type`, `fileUrl`) |
| Create folder | `create_drive_folder` (`folder_name`, optional
  `parent_folder_id`) |
| Copy | `copy_drive_file` (`file_id`, optional `new_name`,
  `parent_folder_id`) |
| Import to Google Doc | `import_to_google_doc` (`file_name` + content /
  path / url) |
| Metadata / move / trash | `update_drive_file` (`file_id`; `name`,
  `add_parents` / `remove_parents`, `trashed`, …) |
| Grant / revoke / transfer | `manage_drive_access` (`action=grant\|
  grant_batch\|update\|revoke\|transfer_owner`, `role`, `share_type`, …) |
| Anyone-with-link toggle | `set_drive_file_permissions` (`link_sharing`
  `off\|reader\|commenter\|writer`) |

Share / public-link / trash / ownership transfer need an explicit verb — see
`google-workspace-safety`.

## Procedure

1. **Search / list first** — `search_drive_files` or `list_drive_items` before
   creating a near-duplicate name in the same folder. Scope Shared Drives with
   `drive_id` / `corpora` when the user named one.
   **Done when** candidate file/folder ids are from MCP, or none match.
2. **Resolve** — pick `file_id` / `folder_id` from results (or verify a
   user-supplied id with get/list). **Done when** every id you will use was
   returned by MCP.
3. **Read or audit** — `get_drive_file_content` for contents;
   `get_drive_file_permissions` / `manage_drive_access` `list` /
   `check_drive_file_public_access` for sharing posture.
   **Done when** you can answer the ask with evidence.
4. **Create / copy / move** — when authorized: prefer copy of a template over
   rebuilding; set `parent_folder_id` intentionally. Trash only with
   `trashed=true` and an explicit delete/trash verb.
   **Done when** MCP returns the new/updated id, or you refused.
5. **Share** — grant the narrowest role (`reader` / `commenter` / `writer`)
   and audience (`user` / `group` / `domain` / `anyone`) the user named. Prefer
   named users over `anyone`. Enable link sharing only with an explicit public
   / anyone-with-link verb.
   **Done when** permissions match the ask and evidence cites MCP.
6. **Evidence** — return file name, id, link when useful, and what changed.
   **Done when** no unauthorized share/trash/transfer ran.

## Defaults

1. Never invent file, folder, permission, or Shared Drive ids.
2. Prefer updating/sharing an existing file over minting a near-duplicate.
3. Prefer named-user grants over domain/anyone discovery.
4. Public / anyone-with-link needs an explicit verb this turn.
5. Downloads/exports: use MCP URL helpers; do not dump binaries into chat.
6. Neighbor object stores / other clouds are out of scope for this plugin.

## Refuse

- Do not trash, broaden sharing, transfer ownership, or set link_sharing on
  without an explicit ask (`google-workspace-safety`).
- Do not claim a file is private without checking permissions / public access.
